  "worked_solution": "In our situation:\n\n- When the door was opened, the temperature *dropped by* ${25}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}$, which is a change of $-{25}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}.$\n\n- When the door was closed, the temperature *rose by* ${25}^{∘}\\,\\text{C},$ which is a change of $+{25}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}.$\n\nThese two changes are *opposite quantities*. When opposite quantities combine, they make $0:$\n\n$$\n-25+25=0\n$$\n\nThis means the *total temperature change* is ${0}^{∘}\\,\\text{C},$ so the temperature returns to its original value.\n\nSo, statements I and III are false, while statement II is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\".",
